   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nwaiving the residency requirement for the comptroller and building inspector\nin the town of Chester, county of Orange",
    "basePrintNo": "S8806",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8806-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §23, Town L; amd §3, Pub Off L",
    "lawSection": "Town Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S8806\n\nSPONSOR: SKOUFIS\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the town law and the public officers law, in relation to\nwaiving the residency requirement for the comptroller and building\ninspector in the town of Chester, county of Orange\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo waive the residency requirement for the comptroller and building\ninspector in the town of Chester, county of Orange.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Amends section 23 of the Chester town law by adding subdivi-\nsion 36.\n\nSection 2: Amends section 3 of the public officers law by adding subdi-\nvision 75.\n\nSection 3: Sets the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation was requested by the Town of Chester. The bill allows\nthe Town of Chester to hire, for the positions of building inspector and\ncomptroller, anyone who resides in the state of New York, so long as\nthey reside in Orange County.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
